{"id":"a2","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":2,"of":19,"title":"Every noun has a gender","titleHe":"זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה","goal":"Tell masculine nouns from feminine ones, and know the exceptions that matter.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Every Hebrew noun is either masculine or feminine, including objects. This isn't decoration: plurals, adjectives and verbs all have to match it, so it's worth learning each noun together with its gender."},{"type":"text","body":"The usual signal is the ending. Nouns ending in ־ָה or ־ֶת are almost always feminine; nouns with no ending are usually masculine."},{"type":"table","caption":"The usual pattern","head":["masculine","feminine"],"rows":[["סֵפֶר — book","מִטָּה — bed"],["שֻׁלְחָן — table","מַחְבֶּרֶת — notebook"],["יֶלֶד — boy","יַלְדָּה — girl"],["כֶּלֶב — dog","מִשְׁפָּחָה — family"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"A short list of feminine nouns carries no ending at all, and they're all common: עִיר city, אֶרֶץ land, יָד hand, רֶגֶל leg, דֶּרֶךְ way, אֶבֶן stone. Learn these six as exceptions and you'll meet few others."}],"vocab":[{"he":"יֶלֶד","en":"boy","translit":"yeled","g":"m"},{"he":"יַלְדָּה","en":"girl","translit":"yalda","g":"f"},{"he":"בַּיִת","en":"house","translit":"bayit","g":"m"},{"he":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","en":"family","translit":"mishpacha","g":"f"},{"he":"עִיר","en":"city","translit":"ir","g":"f"},{"he":"אֶרֶץ","en":"land, country","translit":"erets","g":"f"},{"he":"שֻׁלְחָן","en":"table","translit":"shulchan","g":"m"},{"he":"מַחְבֶּרֶת","en":"notebook","translit":"machberet","g":"f"},{"he":"חַלּוֹן","en":"window","translit":"chalon","g":"m"},{"he":"דֶּלֶת","en":"door","translit":"delet","g":"f"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in, at","boy","village","second"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יֶלֶד","translit":"yeled"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["mum","girl","thief","like this, such a"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יַלְדָּה","translit":"yalda"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["the text read at the Seder","gets up","house","an appointed festival"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בַּיִת","translit":"bayit"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["before (a clause)","nature","a vow","family"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","translit":"mishpacha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["he will speak","problem","city","since then"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עִיר","translit":"ir"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["stands","land, country","grey","grown up"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֶרֶץ","translit":"erets"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["song, poem","wife, woman","table","more, still, another"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שֻׁלְחָן","translit":"shulchan"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אֶרֶץ","land, country"],["שֻׁלְחָן","table"],["מַחְבֶּרֶת","notebook"],["חַלּוֹן","window"],["דֶּלֶת","door"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “boy”?","options":["אָבִיב","יֶלֶד","גָּדוֹל","קָפֶה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["יֶלֶד","boy"],["יַלְדָּה","girl"],["בַּיִת","house"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה","family"],["עִיר","city"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “family”?","options":["מִשְׁפָּחָה","מַכְחִישׁ","שׁוּק","חָתָן"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מִשְׁפָּחָה","יֶלֶד","מַחְבֶּרֶת","חַלּוֹן"],"correct":2,"say":"מַחְבֶּרֶת","he":true},{"type":"read","he":"יַלְדָּה","translit":"yalda","en":"girl"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “notebook”?","options":["שׁוּק","לֵאמֹר","קוֹל","מַחְבֶּרֶת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “window”?","options":["גֶּשֶׁר","אוֹתָהּ","בְּעָיָה","חַלּוֹן"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “boy” in Hebrew","answer":"יֶלֶד","hint":"yeled"}]}